{"_id":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","communityPosts":[{"postText":"The JetBrains Air in IDEs is here – now in Early Access.\nRun multiple agents in parallel, with the freedom to choose your agent.\n\nAll backed by IDE intelligence and tooling to verify agent changes.\nGet started for free*, with Junie Lite configuration: <a href=\"https://jb.gg/air-in-ide-launch\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">jb.gg/air-in-ide-launch</a>\n\n*𝘛𝘦𝘳𝘮𝘴 𝘢𝘯𝘥 𝘤𝘰𝘯𝘥𝘪𝘵𝘪𝘰𝘯𝘴 𝘢𝘱𝘱𝘭𝘺","postId":"UgkxOuKAYvbkOqzwDQ85TqjxtzBYRAUDUjpA","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1790868652085,"voteCount":24,"postContent":{"type":"video","content":{"type":"video","videoId":"i6rrMM92Tow","title":"Air in IDEs: Meet Your New Agentic Workflow","author":"JetBrains","authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","description":"JetBrains Air in IDEs brings agentic development into the IDE you already use. Run your agents of choice in parallel, keep track of what they're doing, and review their results with the full...","viewCount":88055,"published":1790868652085,"lengthSeconds":115,"liveNow":false,"isUpcoming":false,"isPremiere":false,"is4k":false,"is8k":false,"isNew":false,"isVr180":false,"isVr360":false,"is3d":false,"hasCaptions":false}},"commentCount":1,"authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","author":"JetBrains","type":"community"},{"postText":"“No AI companies. No crypto. No work chat on my phone.”\n\nWhen Jake Wharton was looking for his next role, he shared nine personal values, with one caveat: “You don&apos;t need to share them all, but more is better.”\n\nHere’s his list:\n\n1. No “AI.” No AI companies, AI-based products, or forced AI usage for development.\n2. No crypto. Cryptography is good. Cryptocurrencies are bad.\n3. Remote work. Working remotely, with a couple of office visits each year.\n4. Open source. The company uses open source software and publishes its own projects, or wants to start.\n5. Customers over shareholders. The product focuses on providing value to customers, not enriching shareholders.\n6. People over profits. No gig workers or exploitative practices to squeeze every cent from customers.\n7. Small and focused. Doing one thing well is better than trying to be everything to everyone.\n8. Diversity, equity, and inclusion. Distributing opportunity equally takes active work.\n9. Work/life balance. No work chat, email, or code review on his phone.\n\nIn our conversation with Jake, we went through every value: where it came from and how it shaped his job search. And, of course, we asked: did he have to compromise on any of them when he accepted an offer?\n\nWe also talked about Kotlin, Google, and the future of software development with AI.\n\n📸 A few moments from the shoot. In the group photo, from left to right: our showrunner Oxana Mazurchak, Jake Wharton, and our host Vitaly Bragilevsky.\n\nWatch the full interview <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9WjPdgOK-68\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">youtube.com/watch?v=9WjPdgOK-68</a>","postId":"UgkxR1q4e7zM7OP_ffXr4cnnyqF6HCqZLvRe","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789486252085,"voteCount":337,"postContent":{"type":"multiImage","content":[[{"url":"https://yt3.ggpht.com/w8MW_2LoYM2TIbQLIGQinlj0R3HWeUofENnwgciCHU_W6I4uPC2UraI6R0DPaNoxEDSRkwGkyeypdg=s640-c-fcrop64=1,38000000c7ffffff-rw-nd-v1","width":640,"height":640}],[{"url":"https://yt3.ggpht.com/2PqDseBDgfab74C86mL9hpgRa7lGrL0LWcsr-YeCrYr-6cF493OuDDr23NRia_hFjRZt3gk9s9mlHw=s640-c-fcrop64=1,20000000dfffffff-rw-nd-v1","width":640,"height":640}],[{"url":"https://yt3.ggpht.com/Te6bb_xsm-DtmXwNlsg4xxD_d1xiaC-MMWvL3y8mfqYXMQPjh0zd-tmpcEny8LRYg6sOLyJwmfk5bb8=s640-c-fcrop64=1,2c7b0000bc7affff-rw-nd-v1","width":640,"height":640}],[{"url":"https://yt3.ggpht.com/YPiOdYhqOtOr0DfMbZdGW5z4gbnGvaNw2aKgJfQH8J89Gg2nNXHLZAeD463nEyhECOohSUH7rbxC=s640-c-fcrop64=1,20000000dfffffff-rw-nd-v1","width":640,"height":640}]]},"commentCount":20,"authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","author":"JetBrains","type":"community"},{"postText":"Looking for an on-premises alternative to Jira and Confluence? See Atlassian-to-YouTrack migration in action. Join any of these three sessions: in English with the ‪<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCazp8sGTwS_5wYyqg_Z1VYA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">youtube.com/channel/UCazp8sGTwS_5wYyqg_Z1VYA</a> team, a regional webinar in Russian with our certified partner Noventiq, or in Japanese with JetBrains.\n\n🗓️ September 30\n\n📌 Save your seat: <a href=\"https://jb.gg/ytatwytc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">jb.gg/ytatwytc</a>\n\nHere’s what’s on the agenda:\n\n🔵 Migrating projects, users, and data from Jira, Confluence, and Jira Service Management.\n\n🔵 A live migration demo.\n\n🔵 Cost-effective pricing, licensing, and deployment options. Server or Cloud, AI or no AI – you choose!\n\n🔵 Real customer and partner migration stories.","postId":"Ugkxes6i9lAfXR4zSNuMZTm_umaMIkrCeDKe","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789313452085,"voteCount":60,"postContent":{"type":"image","content":[{"url":"https://yt3.ggpht.com/tY38dObOCiIMXYY-pOUCnL4s8CsOXdVAC9tz5Cz87JnsRk-jPnxZGuhqZjs-TwpS5mU0FO2JS0KO_Q=s640-c-fcrop64=1,00000000ffffffff-rw-nd-v1","width":640,"height":640}]},"commentCount":2,"authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","author":"JetBrains","type":"community"},{"postText":"Registration for JetBrains GameDev Day 2026 is open!\n\nTune in on September 28 for practical sessions on AI-assisted Unity and Godot workflows, ECS migrations, C# and C++ debugging, Unreal Engine profiling, large-asset version control, and CI with Rider and TeamCity.\n\nThe free livestream begins at 10:00 am UTC. Watch parties will also take place in Belgrade (co-hosted with DevGAMM) and Limassol, and all sessions will be recorded and available on demand afterward.\n\nRegister here: <a href=\"https://jb.gg/gamedevday2026-registration\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">jb.gg/gamedevday2026-registration</a>","postId":"Ugkx-TYNcZ0UoijqHQ-Ut06VrhUv67_okQ-M","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789313452085,"voteCount":39,"postContent":null,"commentCount":null,"authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","author":"JetBrains","type":"community"},{"postText":"With Jira and Confluence Data Center approaching their end of life, more teams are considering YouTrack as a self-hosted alternative. \n\nThe YouTrack team has created a practical guide featuring expert tips, real customer experiences, and advice from specialized consulting partners who can support your move with a free demo, proof of concept, and more.\n\nRead the guide today: <a href=\"https://jb.gg/ytMIGytc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">jb.gg/ytMIGytc</a>","postId":"Ugkx620Z_ExxQ1-eveVpEIv_xRADAZEclE2i","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789313452085,"voteCount":62,"postContent":{"type":"image","content":[{"url":"https://yt3.ggpht.com/pwhqdezEN4TJ08PCkkW_w5dyVxOmLIJSfhcpoiWFPtF06ieBiCrRRS09LvsS4lIQyNelSg4JvlM3_A=s640-c-fcrop64=1,00000000ffffffff-rw-nd-v1","width":640,"height":640}]},"commentCount":1,"authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","author":"JetBrains","type":"community"},{"postText":"AI is changing not only how developers write code, but also what’s worth learning in the first place.\n\nWe spoke with Ardit Sulce, a Python educator who has taught more than 650,000 students, about which parts of programming are still worth learning the hard way, what can be handed over to AI, and which skills become more valuable as generating code gets easier.\n\nRead the full interview <a href=\"https://jb.gg/academy/interview/ardit-sulce\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">jb.gg/academy/interview/ardit-sulce</a>","postId":"UgkxtzOxi2wpS8pz9hC8uRfzBnHtapjfp_ZJ","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789313452085,"voteCount":109,"postContent":{"type":"image","content":[{"url":"https://yt3.ggpht.com/mdvY-VI9990AJejyuir4940MeA4U2t-Kd47GVBm4RHRcNVN5xhEdXot32kkw6V6m_E1HpNkiEU2x8f0=s640-c-fcrop64=1,00000000ffffffff-rw-nd-v1","width":640,"height":640}]},"commentCount":null,"authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","author":"JetBrains","type":"community"},{"postText":"Looking for a Jira and Confluence alternative? <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCXh8JqbReXsGTqOTHFTwV8g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">youtube.com/channel/UCXh8JqbReXsGTqOTHFTwV8g</a> chose YouTrack for its long-term server commitment, flexibility, and stable pricing. The team migrated marketing automation projects for major retail customers, including REWE and Hagebau.\n\nGet insights from migration experts on importing Jira and Confluence data, handling manual post-migration configuration, and building custom apps: <a href=\"https://jb.gg/cuMSPytc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">jb.gg/cuMSPytc</a>","postId":"UgkxetLEmzDYWeQALAiyQnkVrCqw3D1xcjOH","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789313452085,"voteCount":5,"postContent":{"type":"video","content":{"type":"video","videoId":"ZCWet20q5Ys","title":"MSP AG Case Study | Adopting YouTrack for Project Management and Documentation","author":"YouTrack by JetBrains","authorId":"UCazp8sGTwS_5wYyqg_Z1VYA","description":"Julian Radünz, Team Lead of Professional Services at MSP AG, shares why they chose YouTrack as a self-hosted Jira and Confluence alternative. The team now has one solution for project management...","viewCount":607,"published":1789313452085,"lengthSeconds":86,"liveNow":false,"isUpcoming":false,"isPremiere":false,"is4k":false,"is8k":false,"isNew":false,"isVr180":false,"isVr360":false,"is3d":false,"hasCaptions":false}},"commentCount":null,"authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","author":"JetBrains","type":"community"},{"postText":"AI is lowering the barrier to software development and raising the bar at the same time.\n\nWhat does that mean for junior developers, CS education, and the skills worth learning now?\n\nClara from JetBrains Academy asks two senior developers to weigh in.\nWatch the conversation → <a href=\"https://jb.gg/academy/genz-asks-video\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">jb.gg/academy/genz-asks-video</a>","postId":"Ugkx6xinDp3vFb0JM4OE7JNewQKUiY6XcNAd","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789313452085,"voteCount":16,"postContent":{"type":"video","content":{"type":"video","videoId":"CKAZu63z0xI","title":"Gen Z asks senior developers about the future of programming","author":"JetBrains Academy and Nebius Academy","description":"You’ve seen Clara explain AI and learning. This time, she’s asking the questions.\n\nClara sits down with Andrew Zakonov from Kineto and Denis Volkhonskiy from Nebius to talk about what it’s...","viewCount":43667,"published":1789313452085,"lengthSeconds":4156,"liveNow":false,"isUpcoming":false,"isPremiere":false,"is4k":false,"is8k":false,"isNew":false,"isVr180":false,"isVr360":false,"is3d":false,"hasCaptions":false}},"commentCount":1,"authorId":"UCGp4UBwpTNegd_4nCpuBcow","author":"JetBrains","type":"community"},{"postText":"📣 Join us for the event &apos;Programming Languages Today and Tomorrow&apos;\n▶️ Watch live: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Za1epSDmyH4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">youtube.com/watch?v=Za1epSDmyH4</a>\n\nWe’ll discuss:\n🔹 How programming languages evolve\n🔹 Recent language design trends\n🔹 How programming languages will survive in the age of LLMs\n\nSee you there!","postId":"UgkxmytlRT-bXPjcgnS9C4aoF60VEdg4zJtC","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/wBPpTj2jbdy-ouAuowvSatAxW01MoFxm8mJB0YCljWkoEhw_UV4hjgziTzprMeFYWRUr4uNMrQ=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height