1385,"liveNow":false,"isUpcoming":false,"isStation":false,"isPremiere":false},{"type":"video","videoId":"DyLKYMNPq2w","title":"create,Save any image as a Pattern in photoshop","author":"Everything Terminal","authorId":"UCK2StGMSPgXKWu_CuiVY2bg","viewCount":38000,"published":1413222050820,"lengthSeconds":99,"liveNow":false,"isUpcoming":false,"isStation":false,"isPremiere":false}],"videosTimestamp":{"$$date":1791905474820},"communityPosts":[{"postText":"This was our first episode in the problem solving series, and it was about linked lists in C.\n\nNo shortcuts, no built-in data structures. Just pointers, memory, and the logic that makes it work.\n\nAnd since the whole narration was scripted in a .md file, you&apos;ll pick up a bit of Markdown along the way too. Two skills, one video.\n\n\nDid you enjoy this one? Let me know if I should keep the series going.","postId":"UgkxGK9sNbAYqK9_5_9Jy7WBHIknBA5t7tmj","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1790091052080,"voteCount":4,"postContent":{"type":"video","content":{"type":"video","videoId":"quKdUy2lo80","title":"LeetCode | Reverse Linked List | C | ASMR Coding Session | EP-1","author":"Everything Terminal","authorId":"UCK2StGMSPgXKWu_CuiVY2bg","description":"🎧 Put your headphones on and enjoy this relaxing ASMR coding session! Today, we're solving LeetCode 206: Reverse a Linked List from scratch using the C programming language.\n\nListen to the...","viewCount":826,"published":1789313452080,"lengthSeconds":2963,"liveNow":false,"isUpcoming":false,"isPremiere":false,"is4k":false,"is8k":false,"isNew":false,"isVr180":false,"isVr360":false,"is3d":false,"hasCaptions":false}},"commentCount":null,"authorId":"UCK2StGMSPgXKWu_CuiVY2bg","author":"Everything Terminal","type":"community"},{"postText":"Here&apos;s the video for my latest build: It&apos;s a A beautiful Wordle game written in pure C for the terminal.\n\nIt features the real Wordle color palette, a fancy gradient title, animated letter reveals, and a clear explanation of the tile colors.\n\nNo external libraries. No GUI. Just C, ANSI escape codes, and terminal magic.","postId":"UgkxDciKf45ODGRii4jv9bHg4fQMsqSchBGN","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789486252080,"voteCount":4,"postContent":{"type":"video","content":{"type":"video","videoId":"KKE_xsJOVI4","title":"I Built a Complete Wordle Game in C (It Looks AMAZING in Terminal) | Neovim, tmux & ASMR Coding","author":"Everything Terminal","authorId":"UCK2StGMSPgXKWu_CuiVY2bg","description":"🎧 Put your headphones on and enjoy this relaxing ASMR coding session! Today, we're building a complete Wordle clone from scratch in C, right in the terminal.\n\nListen to the satisfying mechanical...","viewCount":1206,"published":1789313452080,"lengthSeconds":5251,"liveNow":false,"isUpcoming":false,"isPremiere":false,"is4k":false,"is8k":false,"isNew":false,"isVr180":false,"isVr360":false,"is3d":false,"hasCaptions":false}},"commentCount":null,"authorId":"UCK2StGMSPgXKWu_CuiVY2bg","author":"Everything Terminal","type":"community"},{"postText":"New series starting today.\n\nI&apos;m calling it Problem Solving, where I break down coding problems step by step, with real explanations, not just code that magically works.\n\nFirst up: a classic, Linked Lists on LeetCode.\n\nWe&apos;ll go through the problem, build the intuition, and then write the solution together. Broken down step by step.\n\nVideo drops soon.","postId":"UgkxEA0qSGHZNYmdUaZAcYz9RiQb0nafJSKQ","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}],"publishedTime":1789313452080,"voteCount":14,"postContent":null,"commentCount":4,"authorId":"UCK2StGMSPgXKWu_CuiVY2bg","author":"Everything Terminal","type":"community"},{"postText":"Pure C, no libraries, ANSI escape codes for color and styling in the terminal.\nInput handling accepts both a single number (1-9) or row/col like &quot;2 3&quot;, and rejects garbage input or already-taken cells without ever crashing.\nCheck it out!","postId":"UgkxgBqcNta70ZIVQSP3fQCo82dCKyw3xaW1","authorThumbnails":[{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s76-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":76,"height":76},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":48,"height":48},{"url":"https://yt3.googleusercontent.com/cQ4-UiMl2lOe6MmdiI30hXPBuvcRUEYS7l6pCl4qhFKuDZJaF4Ce3ruif7mH3Xhb6H5IRDj8=s32-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj-mo","width":32,"height":32}]